   "subject": "bifactor model",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;font-size:12pt\">Hi, I&#39;m trying to fit a bifactor model. But I have two questions;</span><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">1)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-weight:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:7pt;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">     1) </span></span></b><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">Can the subscales be covariated with each other?<u></u><u></u></span></b></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">I have created some illustrative syntax for the HS dataset below. </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"ES\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">Bifactor.model &lt;- <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"ES\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">&#39;a =~ 3 + 4 + 9 + 17 + 16 + 22 + 27 + 32<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"ES\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">b =~ 1 + 7 + 13 + 23 + 30 + 33 <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"ES\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">c =~  8+ 14 +21+ 24<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">G =~ 3 + 4 + 9 + 17 + 16 + 22 + 27 + 32 + 1 + 7 + 13 + 23 + 30 + 33 + 8+ 14 +21+ 24<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">a ~~ b<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">a ~~ c<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">b ~~ c&#39;<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">2)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-weight:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:7pt;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">  2) </span></span></b><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">It seems that to validate the bifactor model, it is necessary to calculated the omega, Explained Common Variance (ECV) and Percent of Uncontaminated Correlations (PUC). <u></u><u></u></span></b><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>How can </b></span></font><b style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;font-size:16px\">calculated </b><b style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">these indices in R? </b></p><p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><br></span></p><p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">     T</span><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\">hanks in advance!</font></span></p><div style=\"text-align:justify\"><span><br></span></div><p style=\"text-align:justify\"><b style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><br></b></p><p style=\"text-align:justify\"><b style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><br></b></p><p style=\"text-align:justify\"><b style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><br></b></p><p style=\"text-align:justify\"><b style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><br></b></p></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "vlA6_FcoCgAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2018-02-12T14:57:37Z",
   "subject": "Re: bifactor model",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"text-align:justify\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">1)<span style=\"font-weight:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:7pt;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">     1) </span></span></b><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">Can the subscales be covariated with each other?</span></b></p></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>They can, as long as your model is empirically identified.  </div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">2)<span style=\"font-weight:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:7pt;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">  2) </span></span></b><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">It seems that to validate the bifactor model, it is necessary to calculated the omega, Explained Common Variance (ECV) and Percent of Uncontaminated Correlations (PUC). </span></b><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>How can </b></span></font><b style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;font-size:16px\">calculated </b><b style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">these indices in R? </b></p></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Versions of omega are available in the semTools package, using the<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> reliability() </font>function.</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Postdoctoral Researcher, Methods and Statistics</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">UvA web page: <a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792423028472000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0D_W9WBH1EUBs67fetshxv\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "e6D7ZPi1AAAJ",
